---js
{ layout: 'base.njk', permalink: '/credits/', title: 'Credits and licenses for all course content', description: 'Every data source used in the courses, with authors and licenses: HSK 3.0 list, CC-CEDICT, Wiktionary via Kaikki, frequency lists, Tatoeba and Hanzi Writer.', }
---
<p class="crumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / Credits</p>
<h1>Credits and licenses</h1>
<p class="lead">All course content is either written for this site or comes from openly licensed sources, listed below for each course. Example sentences credit their Tatoeba authors on every page where they appear.</p>
<p>The site code is MIT licensed. Grammar lessons written for the site, and word data derived from CC BY-SA sources (CC-CEDICT, Wiktionary), are shared under CC BY-SA 4.0.</p>
{% updated %}
{% for p in lm.packs %}<h2><a href="{{ p.hubUrl }}">{{ p.name }}</a></h2><ul>{% for c in p.credits %}<li><a href="{{ c.url }}" rel="noopener">{{ c.name }}</a>: {{ c.note }} License: <a href="{{ c.licenseUrl }}" rel="noopener license">{{ c.license }}</a>.</li>{% endfor %}</ul>{% endfor %}
<h2 id="audio">Audio</h2>
<p>Every listen button plays a pre-recorded clip. Single words use human recordings from Wikimedia Commons where one exists: <a href="https://lingualibre.org/" rel="noopener">Lingua Libre</a> for every language, plus the <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Chinese_pronunciation" rel="noopener">Shtooka project</a> Mandarin recordings (Beijing and Liaoning speakers) and other CC0, CC BY and CC BY-SA pronunciation files on Commons; each word page names its speaker and license. Some English sentences use openly licensed (CC BY / CC BY-SA) recordings from <a href="https://tatoeba.org/" rel="noopener">Tatoeba</a>, credited below. Everything else is synthesized: Mandarin with <a href="https://huggingface.co/hexgrad/Kokoro-82M-v1.1-zh" rel="noopener">Kokoro-82M v1.1-zh</a> (Apache-2.0), Spanish, English and Brazilian Portuguese with <a href="https://huggingface.co/hexgrad/Kokoro-82M" rel="noopener">Kokoro-82M v1.0</a> (Apache-2.0), other languages with <a href="https://github.com/OHF-Voice/piper1-gpl" rel="noopener">Piper</a> using openly licensed voices. Recordings were trimmed, loudness-normalized and converted to MP3; changed CC BY-SA recordings stay under CC BY-SA.</p>
{% for a in audio %}<h3>{{ a.name }}</h3><ul><li>Synthesized: {{ a.tts.engine or 'Piper' }} voice {{ a.tts.voice }}, {% if (a.tts.engine or 'Piper') == 'Piper' %}trained on a {{ a.tts.license }}{% else %}{{ a.tts.license }}{% endif %} ({{ a.tts.clips }} clips).</li>{% if a.llClips %}<li>Recorded words ({{ a.llClips }}) from Wikimedia Commons by: {% for s in a.speakers %}{{ s.name }} ({{ s.n }}, {{ s.licenses }}){% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}.</li>{% endif %}{% if a.sentClips %}<li>Recorded sentences ({{ a.sentClips }}) from Tatoeba by: {% for s in a.sentSpeakers %}<a href="{{ s.url }}" rel="noopener">{{ s.name }}</a> ({{ s.n }}, {{ s.license }}){% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}.</li>{% endif %}</ul>{% endfor %}
<h2>Software</h2><ul><li><a href="https://github.com/open-spaced-repetition/ts-fsrs">ts-fsrs</a> (MIT) for spaced review scheduling.</li><li><a href="https://hanziwriter.org/">Hanzi Writer</a> (MIT) with stroke data from Make Me a Hanzi (Arphic Public License).</li><li>Engine ideas from <a href="https://github.com/chuma-beep/mathua">Mathua</a> (MIT).</li><li><a href="https://www.11ty.dev/">Eleventy</a> (MIT) builds the site.</li></ul>
